*Damage Evolution, type=ENERGY
9.16e4
** Interface: contact-based cohesive behaviour. There is no cohesive
** element and therefore no cohesive material; the traction-separation
** law, its initiation criterion and its evolution all live on the
** surface interaction. The penalty stiffness used to be left to the
** Abaqus default on the argument that none then had to be invented, which
** turned out to be the wrong call: on the refined mesh the interface mode
** that default creates is too stiff for the stable increment and the wave
** solution drifts asymmetric. --cohesive-stiffness ply sets it from the
** ply moduli instead. See cohesive_stiffness() above.
*Surface Interaction, name=DELAM
